{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Premise validation: a BEHAVIOUR-PRESERVING `reconcile_one` is not available\n\nValidated the goal against current `origin/main` (cc69cc1179) plus the in-flight change for\n`envious-metal-budgie` (Gerrit 1665), which rewrites the doctor's fold. Two independent passes\n(mine and a held-out analysis) reach the same conclusion: sync and the S3 doctor agree on about\nfour lines of graph arithmetic and disagree on every policy that matters. The ticket's AC #1\n(\"no duplicated merge/unrelated-history logic\") cannot be met without policy flags that flip\nsafety-critical branches.\n\n### The blocking divergences\n\n1. **Unrelated-history policy is CONTRADICTORY, not merely different.** `sync._do_reconverge`\n   REFUSES and mutates nothing when there is no common ancestor and the local store already\n   carries events (`sync.py:144-152`, predicate `_carries_ticket_events` at `sync.py:80-104`) —\n   its documented purpose is to avoid grafting an orphan store into the shared tickets branch.\n   The doctor UNIONS unconditionally (`s3_doctor.py` fold), and that is pinned by a held-out\n   test on a non-empty tracker: `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:81-103`\n   (`test_heal_unions_unrelated_history_head`, asserting \"unrelated head discarded\" must not\n   happen). The same input shape must produce opposite outcomes. A shared\n   `allow_unrelated=` parameter would be a safety-critical policy flag, not a knob.\n\n2. **The merge MECHANISM cannot be unified without breaking sync.** After 1665 the doctor folds\n   with `merge-tree --write-tree` + `commit-tree` and deliberately never touches the worktree.\n   Sync cannot do that: its consumers read ticket events off the tracker's WORKTREE FILES\n   (`_engine_support/reads.py:296,312` -> `reducer/_api.py:127-176`, which scans event files off\n   disk and caches to `<ticket_dir>/.cache.json`). A ref-only merge would advance the ref while\n   readers kept seeing pre-merge state — silent staleness. Sync is always the checked-out case,\n   so it can only ever use the `git merge` / `reset --hard` shape.\n\n3. **Failure policy is opposed.** Sync must never raise: `_union_merge` aborts, keeps local and\n   logs a warning (`sync.py:191-196`), and its read path wraps `reconverge` in a bare\n   `except Exception: pass` (`_engine_support/reads.py:253-258`). The doctor must raise —\n   `push_classify.py:189-201` catches `S3DoctorConflict`, logs `exc.hint`, escalates under\n   `strict`, and abandons the push.\n\n4. **Epoch guard asymmetry.** Sync pins the remote ref and refuses across incompatible store\n   epochs via `compat.store_epoch_merge_target` (`sync.py:177-180`). The doctor has no analog\n   and never reads `.store-compat.json`; its heads are immutable `refs/rebar-doctor/<sha>`\n   scratch refs, so only the pinning half is covered incidentally. Adding the guard is a new\n   refusal branch; dropping it is a safety regression.\n\n5. **Cardinality and lock scope differ.** Sync reconciles ONE remote head against HEAD under a\n   lock covering the whole decision (timeout 15, plain `run_git`); the doctor folds N heads with\n   an unborn-tip seeding rule, fetches bundles OUTSIDE the lock, and locks only the fold\n   (timeout 30, `run_git_write`). The doctor's lock placement is pinned by\n   `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:205`.\n\n### What is actually shareable\n\nOnly a classification helper — `merge_class(tip, head) -> ANCESTOR | UNRELATED | DIVERGED`,\nabsorbing two git probes from each side (`sync.py:144,163` and the doctor's equivalents). That\nis roughly four lines of shared surface, and both call sites would still own their merge,\npublish, refusal and failure logic.\n\n### Options for the operator\n\n- **(A) Close as obsolete.** The duplication this ticket targeted was the doctor's copy of the\n  worktree `git merge` policy. After 1665 the doctor no longer has a worktree merge at all, so\n  the thing to de-duplicate is gone.\n- **(B) Thin share only.** Extract `merge_class` and nothing else. Honest but low-value; it\n  trades four duplicated lines for a new cross-module dependency between the store's two most\n  safety-critical healers.\n- **(C) Deep unification.** Genuinely possible, but NOT behaviour-preserving: it requires\n  deciding the contradictory unrelated-history policy, moving sync onto a merge-tree engine plus\n  an explicit worktree sync, and reconciling raise-vs-warn. That is a rewrite of the store's\n  hottest path and needs its own ticket and plan.\n\nRecommending (A), with (B) as a defensible second. Not proceeding without a scope decision,\nbecause every path that satisfies AC #1 as written is behaviour-changing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786560015411342001,"uuid":"6852d00f-3bf0-40ee-ae1b-9f0cc00dce5b"}